import Mathlib
import Submission.NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.Basic
import Submission.NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.LubinTate.EisFactor
import Submission.NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.NormIndex.normIndex_adicCompletion
import Submission.Commons.RingTheory.Henselian.uniformizer_valuation_eq_exp_neg_one
import Submission.Commons.NumberTheory.NumberField.Completion.exists_unramified_extension_of_inertiaDeg
import Submission.Commons.NumberTheory.NumberField.Completion.norm_range_of_ramificationIdx_eq_one
import Submission.Commons.NumberTheory.NumberField.Completion.isCyclic_algEquiv_adicCompletion_of_ramificationIdx_eq_one
import Submission.Commons.NumberTheory.NumberField.Completion.natCard_quotient_units_range_norm_eq_finrank_of_abelian_local

/-!
# The unramified levels of a `p`-adic field, and Honda's reciprocity law

This file is the entry point of the **unramified layer** of the Lubin–Tate chapter, and it records
the chapter's named classical residue, Honda's explicit reciprocity law.

## Why the unramified levels are needed

The Lubin–Tate levels `K_n = F(Λ_n)` are *totally ramified* over `F`; their norm groups are
`⟨π⟩ · U^n` (`HondaReciprocity`), and their index in `Fˣ` is `(q-1)q^{n-1}`.  The cofinality
statement needed for the existence theorem of local class field theory requires the *powers*
`π^{m+1}`, and those are produced by the unramified levels: the norm group of the unramified
extension of degree `m` is `⟨π^m⟩ · U^0`.

## Main definitions

* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.uniformizerUnit` — the uniformiser of `Q.adicCompletion K` as a
  unit;
* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.adicUnits` — the group `U^0 ≅ (Q.adicCompletionIntegers K)ˣ` of
  units of the completion, as a subgroup of `(Q.adicCompletion K)ˣ`;
* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.unramifiedNormGroup` — the group `⟨π^m⟩ · U^0 ≤ Fˣ`, i.e. the
  norm group of the unramified extension of degree `m`;
* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.HondaReciprocity` — Honda's explicit reciprocity law
  `N_{K_n/F} K_nˣ = ⟨π⟩ · U^n` (Serre, *Local Fields*, Ch. XV §5.2; Neukirch, *Algebraic Number
  Theory*, V.5.5), the chapter's named classical residue for the norm-group description of the
  Lubin–Tate levels.

## Conventions

`F = Q.adicCompletion K` for a number field `K` and a finite place `Q` of `K`.  The uniformiser used
throughout is `Commons.RingTheory.Henselian.uniformizer Q`, whose value is `WithZero.exp (-1)`
(`Commons.RingTheory.Henselian.uniformizer_valuation_eq_exp_neg_one`).
-/

open IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum

set_option linter.style.haveILetI false

namespace NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate

universe u v

noncomputable section

/-- **The uniformiser of the completion `Q.adicCompletion K`, as a unit.**

`Commons.RingTheory.Henselian.uniformizer Q` is an irreducible element of the discrete valuation
ring `Q.adicCompletionIntegers K`, hence a nonzero element of `Q.adicCompletion K` (the
fraction field of that ring). -/
def uniformizerUnit (K : Type u) [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (Q : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K)) :
    (Q.adicCompletion K)ˣ :=
  Units.mk0 (Commons.RingTheory.Henselian.uniformizer (R := NumberField.RingOfIntegers K)
      (K := K) Q : Q.adicCompletion K)
    (by
      haveI : IsFractionRing (Q.adicCompletionIntegers K) (Q.adicCompletion K) := inferInstance
      have h0 : Commons.RingTheory.Henselian.uniformizer (R := NumberField.RingOfIntegers K)
          (K := K) Q ≠ 0 :=
        (Commons.RingTheory.Henselian.uniformizer_irreducible (R := NumberField.RingOfIntegers K)
          (K := K) Q).ne_zero
      intro hbad
      exact h0 (IsFractionRing.injective (Q.adicCompletionIntegers K) (Q.adicCompletion K)
        (by simpa using hbad)))

/-- **The units of the completion, as a subgroup of `Fˣ`**: the image of
`(Q.adicCompletionIntegers K)ˣ` in `(Q.adicCompletion K)ˣ`.  This is the group `U^0` of the
chapter's unit filtration, in the form in which it occurs in the norm groups of the unramified
levels. -/
def adicUnits (K : Type u) [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (Q : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K)) :
    Subgroup (Q.adicCompletion K)ˣ :=
  (⊤ : Subgroup (Q.adicCompletionIntegers K)ˣ).map
    (Units.map (algebraMap (Q.adicCompletionIntegers K) (Q.adicCompletion K)).toMonoidHom)

/-- **The norm group of the unramified extension of degree `m`**: the group
`⟨π^m⟩ · U^0 ≤ Fˣ`, where `π = uniformizerUnit K Q` and `U^0 = adicUnits K Q`.

The unramified extension `F_m/F` of degree `m` (for `F = Q.adicCompletion K`) is the extension
generated by a primitive `(q^m - 1)`-st root of unity; its norm group on units is all of `𝒪[F]ˣ`
(norms of units are units, and every unit is a norm because the residue norm of a finite field
extension is surjective) and the norm of a uniformiser is a uniformiser, so
`N_{F_m/F} F_mˣ = ⟨π^m⟩ · 𝒪[F]ˣ` (Serre, *Local Fields*, Ch. V §2). -/
def unramifiedNormGroup (K : Type u) [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (Q : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K)) (m : ℕ) :
    Subgroup (Q.adicCompletion K)ˣ :=
  Subgroup.zpowers (uniformizerUnit K Q ^ m) ⊔ adicUnits K Q

/-- **Honda's explicit reciprocity law** (the chapter's named classical residue).

For a uniformiser `π` of a nonarchimedean local field `F` with residue cardinality `q`, and a
filtration `U` of `Fˣ` (in applications the higher unit filtration `U^n = 1 + 𝔪^n`), the norm group
of the `n`-th Lubin–Tate level `K_n = F(Λ_n)` — the field generated by the `π^n`-torsion points of
the Lubin–Tate formal group of `π` — is

`N_{K_n/F} K_nˣ = ⟨π⟩ · U^n`   for every `n ≥ 1`.

This is Serre, *Local Fields*, Ch. XV §5.2, and Neukirch, *Algebraic Number Theory*, V.5.5.  The
level is `LTLevel F (π : F) q n`, the intermediate field of `AlgebraicClosure F` generated by the
division points (`LubinTate/EisFactor.lean`), and its norm group is
`NK.LocalReciprocity.normGroup F ↥(LTLevel F (π : F) q n)`.

**What is proved from this hypothesis.**  Everything else in the construction: the two-parameter
levels `E_{m,n} = F_{m+1} · K_{n+1}` (the unramified extension of degree `m+1` composed with the
Lubin–Tate level), their norm groups `⟨π^{m+1}⟩ · U^{n+1}`, and the *existence theorem*
`NK.LocalCFT.ExistenceTheoremAbstract F` (every finite-index subgroup of `Fˣ` contains the norm
group of some finite abelian extension).  The remaining classical input of the delivery is
`NK.LocalArtin.KernelCondition F F'` (the norm residue symbol with the correct kernels), which is
*not* implied by `HondaReciprocity`. -/
def HondaReciprocity (F : Type u) [Field F] (π : Fˣ) (U : ℕ → Subgroup Fˣ) (q : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n → NK.LocalReciprocity.normGroup F ↥(LTLevel F (π : F) q n) =
      Subgroup.zpowers π ⊔ U n

end

end NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate
